  "limitations": [
    "Fixtures inject integer ticks and already projected durations. They do not execute a fractional protobuf Action projection with an actual subsecond process launch.",
    "Explicit zero, omitted infinite timeout and maximum finite Action duration are not added fixture cases. Existing saturating deadline arithmetic and u64::MAX require separate headroom/admission qualification.",
    "At u64::MAX a strict finite execution deadline cannot be crossed; independently saturated progress/interest windows retain their existing semantics. This is not proof that a finite overflow was safely classified as infinity.",
    "Unit, sampling/proposal-version and provenance binding are still absent from canonical bootstrap. Arbitrary injected experimental ticks or direct reducer proposals do not inherit the conditional elapsed-time proof.",
    "Independent progress, interest loss, cancellation and worker replacement can revoke before the requested execution duration. No uninterrupted-execution or minimum policy-window promise is established.",
    "Expiry does not prove process quiescence or release physical reservations; only existing matching cleanup or other separately qualified settlement does.",
    "No production constructor activation, migration compatibility, wall-time upper bound, exhaustive schedule claim or reviewer execution counts."
